<body>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">🧊 Fridge Cooking Guide</div>
    <h1>What's in my fridge? 60+ genius recipes to cook tonight</h1>
    <p>No grocery run needed — just what's already hiding behind the mustard jar.</p>
    <div class="hero-emoji-row">🍳 🥑 🍅 🧀 🥦</div>
  </div>
</header>
<svg class="wave" viewBox="0 0 1440 60" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path fill="#FFF6E9" d="M0,32 C240,60 480,0 720,20 C960,40 1200,60 1440,24 L1440,60 L0,60 Z"/></svg>

<main>

  <section class="band band-cream">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Why it matters</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Fridge cooking is the smartest skill you'll ever learn</h2>
      <p>It's 6:47pm, you're starving, and you open the fridge thinking "there's nothing to eat." Except there usually <em>is</em> something — half an onion, a few eggs, a nub of cheese. That's not nothing. That's dinner waiting to happen. 🎉</p>
      <div class="chip-grid">
        <div class="chip"><span class="chip-emoji">💰</span><strong>Save money</strong><span class="sub">Stop tossing groceries you already paid for.</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><span class="chip-emoji">🌍</span><strong>Cut food waste</strong><span class="sub">Wilted veg is one of the biggest culprits.</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><span class="chip-emoji">⏱️</span><strong>Save time</strong><span class="sub">No traffic, no checkout lines.</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><span class="chip-emoji">🧠</span><strong>Cook better</strong><span class="sub">Improvising is how real chefs train.</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><span class="chip-emoji">😌</span><strong>Less stress</strong><span class="sub">No more scrolling recipe blogs at 7pm.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tip-box"><span class="label">Pro tip 💡</span> — Do a 2-minute "fridge audit" before you cook. Whatever's closest to going bad should be your starting point, not the ingredients with a month of shelf life left.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Rule #1</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🍳 The "almost anything" egg method</h2>
      <p>Eggs are the most versatile fridge ingredient on the planet, and they're usually sitting right there in the door. If you have eggs and literally anything else, you have a meal.</p>
      <div class="formula-box">🍳 <strong>The formula:</strong> 2–3 eggs + 1 cup chopped vegetables + a handful of cheese (optional) + salt, pepper, whatever spices you have = dinner.</div>
      <ul class="recipe-list">
        <li><strong>Fridge frittata</strong> — whisk eggs over sautéed veg in a hot pan, cook low and slow, finish under the broiler 2 minutes</li>
        <li><strong>Fried rice omelet</strong> — scramble eggs with leftover rice, soy sauce, and any chopped veg</li>
        <li><strong>Shakshuka-style eggs</strong> — simmer tomatoes with garlic and spices, crack in eggs, cover and poach</li>
        <li><strong>Egg fried everything</strong> — any leftover roasted vegetable, chopped and fried with eggs and soy sauce</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-green">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Rule #2</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🍜 Turn leftover rice or pasta into a new meal</h2>
      <p>Cooked rice and pasta are secretly some of the most valuable things in your fridge — they act as a blank canvas for whatever else needs using up.</p>
      <h3>🍚 Leftover rice ideas</h3>
      <ul class="recipe-list">
        <li><strong>Fried rice</strong> — any protein + any vegetable + soy sauce, sesame oil, garlic</li>
        <li><strong>Rice bowls</strong> — topped with a fried egg, hot sauce, and whatever veg needs using</li>
        <li><strong>Stuffed peppers</strong> — rice, cheese, and canned beans or ground meat</li>
        <li><strong>Rice soup</strong> — simmered in broth with roasted vegetables and shredded chicken</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>🍝 Leftover pasta ideas</h3>
      <ul class="recipe-list">
        <li><strong>Pasta frittata</strong> — mix cold pasta with eggs and cheese, pan-fry like a cake</li>
        <li><strong>Pasta salad</strong> — olive oil, vinegar, raw veg, canned tuna or beans</li>
        <li><strong>Baked pasta</strong> — any sauce and cheese, baked until bubbly</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="tip-box"><span class="label">Rule of thumb 🎯</span> — Any cooked starch + protein + vegetable + sauce = a legitimate meal. This formula alone solves 80% of "what's for dinner" panics.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-red">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Rescue mission</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🥕 The sad vegetable drawer rescue guide</h2>
      <p>Every fridge has one: the drawer where things go to be forgotten. Wilting spinach, a rubbery carrot, half a cabbage. Here's how to save them all. 🥬🥕🍄</p>
      <ul class="recipe-list">
        <li><strong>Wilting greens</strong> → sauté with garlic, fold into pasta, eggs, or grain bowls</li>
        <li><strong>Soft carrots or celery</strong> → roast with olive oil, or simmer into soup</li>
        <li><strong>Limp broccoli or cauliflower</strong> → roast at high heat until crispy — heat fixes almost everything</li>
        <li><strong>Half an onion, pepper, mushrooms</strong> → the base of any stir-fry, soup, or omelet</li>
        <li><strong>Overripe tomatoes</strong> → simmer into a quick sauce with garlic and olive oil</li>
        <li><strong>Sad herbs</strong> → blend with oil, garlic, nuts and parmesan into a quick pesto</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="formula-box">🍲 <strong>One-pot fridge clean-out soup:</strong> chop every vegetable that's about to turn, sauté in a pot with olive oil, add broth, simmer 20 minutes, season generously. Add leftover rice, pasta, or beans to bulk it up.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-cream">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Emergency kit</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🧀 The cheese & bread emergency kit</h2>
      <p>If your fridge has cheese and your pantry has bread, you're never more than 10 minutes from a satisfying meal.</p>
      <ul class="recipe-list">
        <li><strong>Grilled cheese upgrades</strong> — caramelized onion, sliced apple, roasted veg, or a fried egg inside</li>
        <li><strong>Quesadillas</strong> — cheese + tortilla + anything, folded and pan-fried</li>
        <li><strong>Cheesy toast</strong> — broil bread with cheese and any topping for 3 minutes</li>
        <li><strong>Croque Madame</strong> — grilled cheese topped with a fried egg 🍳</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Combos that never fail</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🥫 Pantry + fridge combo meals</h2>
      <p>Keep these staples on hand and you'll never truly be stuck:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Pantry staple</th><th>Combine with</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Canned beans 🫘</td><td>Any veg + spices</td><td>Hearty bean stew or taco filling</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Canned tomatoes 🍅</td><td>Garlic + pasta</td><td>15-minute pasta sauce</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Broth/bouillon 🍲</td><td>Any veg + protein</td><td>Instant soup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tortillas 🌯</td><td>Anything</td><td>Tacos, quesadillas, wraps</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Soy sauce + rice vinegar 🥢</td><td>Any veg + protein</td><td>Stir-fry</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Curry paste/powder 🍛</td><td>Coconut milk + veg</td><td>Curry in 20 minutes</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-green">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Give it a second life</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🍗 What to do with random leftover protein</h2>
      <p>Half a rotisserie chicken, two slices of ham, a cup of ground beef — protein is usually the most expensive thing in your fridge, so it deserves a second life.</p>
      <ul class="recipe-list">
        <li><strong>Shredded/diced chicken</strong> → quesadillas, fried rice, chicken salad, soup, grain bowls</li>
        <li><strong>Ground meat</strong> → tacos, pasta sauce, stuffed peppers, fried rice</li>
        <li><strong>Ham or deli meat</strong> → fried rice, frittata, sandwiches, carbonara-style pasta</li>
        <li><strong>Canned tuna or salmon</strong> → pasta, salad, sandwiches, rice bowls</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-white">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">Try tonight</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">🥑 5 full "fridge-only" recipes</h2>
      <div class="recipe-grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>🍚 Kitchen sink fried rice</h3><p>Cold rice + any chopped veg + any diced protein + 2 eggs + soy sauce + garlic + sesame oil. Fry rice till crispy, push aside, scramble eggs, mix, season.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>🍲 Everything-but-the-kitchen-sink soup</h3><p>Sauté onion, garlic, any veg. Add broth. Simmer 20 min. Add cooked grain, pasta, or beans. Season generously, finish with lemon or vinegar.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>🥙 The "whatever's left" wrap</h3><p>Tortilla + spread + protein + cheese + any veg + hot sauce. Roll tight, pan-sear 2 min a side for crunch.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>🍝 5-ingredient fridge pasta</h3><p>Pasta + olive oil + garlic + any veg + parmesan. Boil pasta, sauté veg, toss with pasta water, top with cheese.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>🥗 The big salad that's actually a meal</h3><p>Greens + leftover protein + roasted or raw veg + cheese + nuts + a simple oil-and-vinegar dressing.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-dark">
    <div class="container cta-box">
      <h2>🤖 Still staring at the fridge?</h2>
      <p>Tell Fridge Chef exactly what's in your fridge right now, and get real meal ideas in seconds — no scrolling, no guessing, no 8 open tabs. It's the fastest way to turn "there's nothing to eat" into "dinner's ready." 🍽️✨</p>
